From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 11:56:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] libxl/arm: one SPI per virtio-pci slot instead of INTA-D

With four SPIs the interrupt-map wraps (irq = irq_first + ((pin + slot) %
num_irqs)), so slots 1&5, 2&6, 3&7 and 4&8 share one level-triggered SPI each.
Measured in DomA with eight virtio-pci devices (2026-08-24):

    14: 14437  Level  virtio0, virtio4   (blk 01   + tablet 05)
    15:   599  Level  virtio1, virtio5   (vsock 02 + net1 06)
    16: 30570  Level  virtio2, virtio6   (serial 03+ gpu 07)
    17:   155  Level  virtio7, virtio3   (net0 04  + snd 08)

virtio-blk and virtio-net recover from a lost interrupt on the next kick, but
virtio-snd's used-buffer interrupt is its only wake-up source, so one lost
interrupt stalls playback permanently. The guest cannot use MSI instead: this
SoC has a GIC-400 (GICv2, no ITS) and Xen emulates no GICv2m frame for guests.

Hand out one SPI per slot, sixteen per host, and widen interrupt-map-mask to
four device-number bits. Sixteen rather than eight because the hardware decoder
adds virtio-media at slot 09.0, and at eight the map wraps again and slot 9
lands on slot 1 -- virtio-blk, the rootfs. GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_FIRST..LAST is
32 SPIs, so at sixteen a guest can have two virtio-pci hosts: libxl allocates
them per guest, one per backend domain, and every guest here has one, DomD. The
SPI BUILD_BUG_ON becomes a bound rather than an equality, and a runtime guard
rejects a third host instead of letting it overlap. The interrupt-map keeps an
entry per slot for each of the four INTx pins rather than one per SPI, since a
PCI function has no pin beyond INTD.

Requires the matching qemu change (one SPI per virtio-pci slot). An older qemu
rejects num_irqs != GPEX_NUM_IRQS and the device model fails to spawn, so the
two must be deployed together.

This is the two steps the bring-up took (4 -> 8 -> 16) as one change: eight was
never shipped, and a guest DT generated at eight pairs with no libxl here.
Rebased onto Xen 4.22: the prefetch-window equality the first step relaxed had
already become a bound in 4.22-0009 (the Venus 256 MiB window), so only the SPI
equality is touched.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / BSP-layer delta]
---
--- a/tools/libs/light/libxl_arm.c
+++ b/tools/libs/light/libxl_arm.c
@@ -43,7 +43,46 @@
  * domain), so nothing that works today stops working.
  */
 #define VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_PREFETCH_MEM_SIZE   xen_mk_ullong(0x10000000)
-#define VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_SPIS            4
+/*
+ * One SPI per PCI slot instead of the four INTA-D lines, and sixteen of them.
+ *
+ * With 4 the interrupt-map wraps (irq = irq_first + ((pin + slot) % num_irqs)),
+ * so slots 1&5, 2&6, 3&7 and 4&8 share one level-triggered SPI each. Measured
+ * in DomA with eight virtio-pci devices (2026-08-24):
+ *     14: 14437  Level  virtio0, virtio4   (blk 01   + tablet 05)
+ *     15:   599  Level  virtio1, virtio5   (vsock 02 + net1 06)
+ *     16: 30570  Level  virtio2, virtio6   (serial 03+ gpu 07)
+ *     17:   155  Level  virtio7, virtio3   (net0 04  + snd 08)
+ * virtio-blk and virtio-net recover from a lost interrupt on the next kick, but
+ * virtio-snd's used-buffer interrupt is its only wake-up source: the shared line
+ * stopped delivering after 155 interrupts and playback stalled permanently.
+ *
+ * Sixteen, not eight: DomA already fills slots 01.0..08.0 and the hardware
+ * decoder adds virtio-media at 09.0. At eight the map wraps again and slot 9
+ * lands on slot 1's line -- virtio-blk, the rootfs. A decode session waits on
+ * DQBUF and on the event queue, so a dropped completion stalls it with no kick
+ * to recover it, unlike virtio-blk.
+ *
+ * Slot N -> SPI_FIRST + N for every slot that exists, no wrap:
+ *   01 blk  02 vsock  03 serial  04 net  05 tablet
+ *   06 net1 07 gpu    08 snd     09 media
+ *
+ * The window is unchanged and sufficient: SPI_FIRST..LAST is 32 SPIs = two
+ * hosts of 16. A guest gets one host per backend domain (alloc_virtio_pci_host()
+ * allocates them per guest), so that is two backend domains per guest, and every
+ * guest here has one, DomD. A third host is rejected by the runtime guard in
+ * alloc_virtio_pci_host() rather than silently overlapping.
+ *
+ * The guest cannot use MSI instead: this SoC has a GIC-400 (GICv2, no ITS) and
+ * Xen emulates no GICv2m frame for guests, so the guest only has legacy INTx.
+ *
+ * Requires the matching qemu change (one SPI per virtio-pci slot). An older
+ * qemu rejects num_irqs != GPEX_NUM_IRQS and the device model fails to spawn,
+ * so the two must be deployed together.
+ */
+#define VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_SPIS            16
+/* INTA..INTD: the interrupt-map has an entry per slot for each of them. */
+#define VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_PINS            4
 #define VIRTIO_PCI_MAX_HOSTS                8
 #define VIRTIO_PCI_MAX_PREFETCH_HOSTS       \
     (GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_PREFETCH_MEM_SIZE / VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_PREFETCH_MEM_SIZE)
@@ -134,7 +173,13 @@ static int alloc_virtio_pci_host(libxl__gc *gc,
     BUILD_BUG_ON(VIRTIO_PCI_MAX_PREFETCH_HOSTS < 1);
     BUILD_BUG_ON(GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_PREFETCH_MEM_SIZE %
                  VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_PREFETCH_MEM_SIZE);
-    BUILD_BUG_ON(VIRTIO_PCI_MAX_HOSTS !=
+    /*
+     * The SPI window now holds fewer hosts than the ECAM and MEM windows do
+     * (NUM_SPIS was raised to 16), so this is a bound, not an equality: 32 SPIs
+     * at 16 each is 2 hosts. The per-host range is checked against SPI_LAST in
+     * alloc_virtio_pci_host() below.
+     */
+    BUILD_BUG_ON(VIRTIO_PCI_MAX_HOSTS <
                  (GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_LAST - GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_FIRST) / VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_SPIS);
 
     if (*num_hosts > VIRTIO_PCI_MAX_HOSTS)
@@ -189,6 +234,13 @@ static int alloc_virtio_pci_host(libxl__gc *gc,
     hosts[i].irq_first = GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_FIRST +
         i * VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_SPIS;
     hosts[i].num_irqs = VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_SPIS;
+    if (hosts[i].irq_first + hosts[i].num_irqs - 1 > GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_LAST) {
+        LOG(ERROR, "virtio-pci host #%u SPI range %u..%u exceeds %u",
+            i, hosts[i].irq_first,
+            hosts[i].irq_first + hosts[i].num_irqs - 1,
+            GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_LAST);
+        return ERROR_INVAL;
+    }
 
     *host_id = hosts[i].id;
 
@@ -1127,12 +1179,12 @@ static int create_virtio_pci_irq_map(libxl__gc *gc, void *fdt,
         return res;
 
     cells = res;
-    len = sizeof(uint32_t) * host->num_irqs * host->num_irqs *
+    len = sizeof(uint32_t) * host->num_irqs * VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_PINS *
           (PCI_IRQ_MAP_MIN_STRIDE + cells);
     irq_map = full_irq_map = libxl__malloc(gc, len);
 
     for (slot = 0; slot < host->num_irqs; slot++) {
-        for (pin = 0; pin < host->num_irqs; pin++) {
+        for (pin = 0; pin < VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_PINS; pin++) {
             uint32_t irq = host->irq_first + ((pin + slot) % host->num_irqs);
             unsigned int i = 0;
 
@@ -1162,8 +1214,14 @@ static int create_virtio_pci_irq_map(libxl__gc *gc, void *fdt,
     res = fdt_property(fdt, "interrupt-map", full_irq_map, len);
     if (res) return res;
 
+    /*
+     * Mask FOUR device-number bits (slots 0-15) to match
+     * VIRTIO_PCI_HOST_NUM_SPIS = 16. PCI_DEVFN(3, 0) masked two bits, so slot 8
+     * folded onto slot 0 and every line was shared; three bits would be right
+     * for 8 SPIs but folds slot 9 (virtio-media) onto slot 1 (virtio-blk).
+     */
     res = fdt_property_values(gc, fdt, "interrupt-map-mask", 4,
-                              PCI_DEVFN(3, 0) << 8, 0, 0, 0x7);
+                              PCI_DEVFN(15, 0) << 8, 0, 0, 0x7);
     if (res) return res;
 
     return 0;
